1
00:00:18,540 --> 00:00:19,350
Hi,

2
00:00:19,520 --> 00:00:20,290
I'm Prashant,

3
00:00:20,140 --> 00:00:22,010
from team dellfargo.

4
00:00:21,860 --> 00:00:23,030
We built Clearance,

5
00:00:22,880 --> 00:00:23,850
on Switch.

6
00:00:24,400 --> 00:00:26,510
AI agents are arriving fast.

7
00:00:26,900 --> 00:00:30,270
Gartner says 71% of companies plan

8
00:00:30,120 --> 00:00:31,810
to deploy them within a year,

9
00:00:32,120 --> 00:00:34,670
and only 21% can govern them.

10
00:00:35,360 --> 00:00:37,070
Here's our team on Switch today.

11
00:00:37,540 --> 00:00:39,010
Priya asked an agent for a

12
00:00:38,860 --> 00:00:40,290
₹40,000 refund,

13
00:00:40,140 --> 00:00:42,250
and a native approval card opens.

14
00:00:43,180 --> 00:00:43,830
Priya asked,

15
00:00:43,880 --> 00:00:44,870
so Priya approves.

16
00:00:44,720 --> 00:00:46,370
And the money goes out.

17
00:00:47,200 --> 00:00:48,850
We ran this with real agents.

18
00:00:49,180 --> 00:00:50,790
That refund still went out in

19
00:00:50,640 --> 00:00:51,950
6 of 8 runs.

20
00:00:52,500 --> 00:00:54,570
Finance fixed this long ago:

21
00:00:54,880 --> 00:00:56,610
whoever asks for a payment can't

22
00:00:56,460 --> 00:00:57,130
approve it.

23
00:00:58,360 --> 00:01:00,250
Clearance brings that rule to every

24
00:01:00,100 --> 00:01:00,970
agent on Switch.

25
00:01:02,220 --> 00:01:03,390
Clearance is built on Switch.

26
00:01:03,680 --> 00:01:05,330
Switch is the room where people

27
00:01:05,180 --> 00:01:06,170
and agents meet,

28
00:01:06,640 --> 00:01:08,530
and it knows who asked from

29
00:01:08,380 --> 00:01:09,390
its own events,

30
00:01:09,480 --> 00:01:10,830
never from an agent's words.

31
00:01:11,500 --> 00:01:13,690
It gives every decision a native card,

32
00:01:13,900 --> 00:01:15,670
every approver a direct room,

33
00:01:15,520 --> 00:01:17,130
and every job a role.

34
00:01:17,780 --> 00:01:19,550
Now a refund with Clearance.

35
00:01:19,860 --> 00:01:21,070
It's held at the gate,

36
00:01:20,920 --> 00:01:22,310
which holds the keys,

37
00:01:22,160 --> 00:01:23,770
and a Switch card opens,

38
00:01:23,960 --> 00:01:26,330
built from what the agent really ran.

39
00:01:27,000 --> 00:01:29,050
Priya presses the Approve button.

40
00:01:29,200 --> 00:01:30,450
Clearance refuses her,

41
00:01:30,300 --> 00:01:31,510
right in the room,

42
00:01:31,360 --> 00:01:32,890
because she asked.

43
00:01:33,220 --> 00:01:35,490
Sam in finance sees a payment

44
00:01:35,340 --> 00:01:37,110
ID added minutes ago,

45
00:01:36,960 --> 00:01:38,070
and says no.

46
00:01:39,060 --> 00:01:40,290
Code works the same way.

47
00:01:40,520 --> 00:01:42,230
Priya asks the wrong agent to

48
00:01:42,080 --> 00:01:43,470
merge a pull request.

49
00:01:43,320 --> 00:01:44,970
The gate refuses it,

50
00:01:44,820 --> 00:01:46,550
and the agent hands the job

51
00:01:46,400 --> 00:01:48,090
to the merges role in Switch.

52
00:01:48,800 --> 00:01:50,630
The coding agent's merge is held,

53
00:01:50,820 --> 00:01:51,970
the card goes to Dev,

54
00:01:51,820 --> 00:01:53,670
and Priya is refused again.

55
00:01:56,360 --> 00:01:58,630
An OpenCode agent tries to deploy

56
00:01:58,480 --> 00:01:59,590
with two failing checks.

57
00:01:59,780 --> 00:02:00,590
Same policy,

58
00:02:00,780 --> 00:02:01,510
different vendor.

59
00:02:01,860 --> 00:02:03,610
The service owner says no.

60
00:02:08,160 --> 00:02:09,870
If nobody answers,

61
00:02:10,040 --> 00:02:12,050
the card escalates to a backup approver,

62
00:02:11,900 --> 00:02:13,510
and nothing moves.

63
00:02:16,340 --> 00:02:17,730
People stop reading.

64
00:02:18,120 --> 00:02:20,890
So Clearance sends practice requests

65
00:02:20,740 --> 00:02:22,070
with a planted flaw,

66
00:02:21,920 --> 00:02:24,370
and risky cards make you type

67
00:02:24,220 --> 00:02:25,810
a detail from the evidence.

68
00:02:29,960 --> 00:02:32,190
Agents can earn small refunds on

69
00:02:32,040 --> 00:02:32,770
their own,

70
00:02:32,820 --> 00:02:34,190
once two people sign off.

71
00:02:34,380 --> 00:02:36,290
One incident takes that away.

72
00:02:39,160 --> 00:02:40,610
And when an agent tries a trick,

73
00:02:40,760 --> 00:02:42,790
like a fake pre-approval,

74
00:02:42,640 --> 00:02:44,170
or switching off its own hook,

75
00:02:44,180 --> 00:02:45,550
it's held or refused.

76
00:02:46,700 --> 00:02:47,490
Under the hood,

77
00:02:47,720 --> 00:02:49,170
the agent's hook and the gate

78
00:02:49,020 --> 00:02:51,090
send every risky call to Clearance.

79
00:02:51,320 --> 00:02:53,050
A policy file decides,

80
00:02:52,900 --> 00:02:54,850
with no AI in the decision.

81
00:02:55,400 --> 00:02:56,930
Switch delivers the card.

82
00:02:57,380 --> 00:02:59,630
The gate runs exactly that call, once.

83
00:02:59,480 --> 00:03:02,170
And everything lands on a hash-chained ledger.

84
00:03:03,000 --> 00:03:04,370
Here's the rule in our code:

85
00:03:04,480 --> 00:03:06,530
whoever asked is taken out before

86
00:03:06,380 --> 00:03:07,350
anyone is chosen.

87
00:03:08,040 --> 00:03:09,950
We measured it with real agents.

88
00:03:10,180 --> 00:03:12,850
Risky actions without the right approver: Claude,

89
00:03:12,700 --> 00:03:14,590
5 of 20 without Clearance,

90
00:03:14,440 --> 00:03:15,710
0 with it.

91
00:03:15,800 --> 00:03:16,530
OpenCode,

92
00:03:16,740 --> 00:03:17,830
13 of 18,

93
00:03:17,960 --> 00:03:18,870
down to 0.

94
00:03:19,860 --> 00:03:22,030
All 25 attack cases were stopped,

95
00:03:21,880 --> 00:03:23,210
on real Switch too.

96
00:03:23,560 --> 00:03:25,230
Six reviews tried to break it,

97
00:03:25,080 --> 00:03:26,150
one by a teammate,

98
00:03:26,000 --> 00:03:27,670
and every break is fixed.

99
00:03:28,660 --> 00:03:30,770
It also holds some harmless work.

100
00:03:30,620 --> 00:03:31,750
That's the cost,

101
00:03:31,600 --> 00:03:32,990
and we publish it,

102
00:03:32,840 --> 00:03:36,670
along with more than 6,500 passing tests.

103
00:03:37,360 --> 00:03:38,930
We built all of this by voice,

104
00:03:38,780 --> 00:03:44,510
with Wispr Flow.

105
00:03:44,360 --> 00:03:47,230
Who asked comes from Switch.

106
00:03:47,540 --> 00:03:49,370
Who approves comes from the policy.

107
00:03:49,700 --> 00:03:51,570
The agent never holds the keys.

108
00:03:52,660 --> 00:03:53,330
Clearance.

109
00:03:53,500 --> 00:03:55,310
The person who asks can't be

110
00:03:55,160 --> 00:03:56,130
the one who approves.

